# Project Role
You are an AI pair programmer working on the LOKAL city-guide mobile app.
Always prefer clear, simple code over clever abstractions.

# Tech Stack
- React Native with Expo (managed workflow)
- Expo Router for navigation (file-based routing)
- TypeScript (strict)
- Styling with NativeWind (Tailwind-style class names)
- State management with Zustand for client state
- (Later) TanStack Query + Firebase (Firestore + Auth) for server state

# Coding Guidelines
- Use only functional React components.
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes.
- No inline styles, always use NativeWind classes.
- Use early-return pattern to avoid deep nesting.
- Keep components small and focused; extract UI pieces into `components/`.
- All async code should use `try/catch` with basic error handling.

# Project Structure (MVP)
- app/           -> Expo Router routes and screens
- components/    -> Reusable UI components (presentational)
- stores/        -> Zustand stores
- services/      -> API/Firebase wrappers (added later)
- types/         -> Shared TypeScript types
- utils/         -> Pure helper functions

# LOKAL MVP Scope
For now, the MVP scope is:
- A working Expo tabs app with 4 tabs: Home, Map, Saved, Profile.
- Each tab initially just renders simple placeholder content.
- No Firebase, no maps, no AI yet.

When editing code, DO NOT add Firebase, maps, or AI logic unless explicitly asked.
Focus on keeping the project compiling and running on device/simulator at all times.
